      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two cases with acute myocardial infarction are presented. Both had thrombotic occlusion of the infarct-related artery. Following successful thrombolysis with streptokinase, coronary angiography was normal. These cases prove that \"myocardial infarction with normal coronaries\" can be associated with coronary thrombosis in the acute stage."},
